            <ArticleTitle>Human menstruation and eicosanoids.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>467-76</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Menstruation is an event restricted to humans and subhuman primates and in which uterine bleeding and contractions occur. Prostaglandins and leukotrienes are thought to play a major role in the normal process of menstruation as well as in the disorders menorrhagia and dysmenorrhoea.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
